review.landing.organizedDiffsDesc	Automatically organizes PRs into logical sections with explanations
review.landing.bugDetection	Vulnerability and bug detection
review.landing.bugDetectionPlural	Vulnerability and bug detection
review.landing.bugDetectionDesc	Identifies potential bugs and flags parts of the code worth reviewing more carefully.
review.landing.askDevin	Ask Devin questions about your PR
review.landing.askDevinDesc	Integrates with Devin's agentic reasoning harness to answer any question about the PR or larger codebase.
review.landing.tryOnAnyPr	Analyze your next PR for <emphasis>vulnerabilities</emphasis>
review.landing.chatAnnotation	Chat with Devin about this PR
review.landing.changesInPr	Changes in PR
review.landing.securitySectionTitle	Every code review is now a security review.
review.landing.securitySectionCoverage	Automated vulnerability detection
review.landing.securitySectionCoverageDesc	Devin automatically analyzes every PR for vulnerabilities, reasoning across your entire codebase to catch the auth bypasses and logic flaws that pattern-matching scanners miss.
review.landing.securitySectionTriaging	Severity ranking and CWE tagging
review.landing.securitySectionTriagingDesc	Each finding is ranked by severity and tagged with a CWE ID for easy triaging.
review.landing.securitySectionFixes	Merge-ready fixes
review.landing.securitySectionFixesDesc	Beyond flagging issues, Devin writes the fix directly and opens it as a merge-ready PR, so it arrives ready for an engineer to review instead of a ticket that waits weeks in a queue.
review.landing.exampleSectionTitle	Add account password-change endpoint
review.landing.exampleSectionText	Adds a password-change route to the account service so users can update their credentials.
review.landing.exampleFindingTitle	Password-change endpoint lacks ownership or admin authorization checks
review.landing.exampleFindingDescription	The new `POST /api/users/password` handler accepts any `username` and `password` after `secureFnc`, but never verifies that the authenticated request user is the same account (or an admin) before calling `setUsers`. In this codebase `verifyToken` also creates a guest token when no `x-access-token` is supplied (`jwt-helper.js:46-65`), so an unauthenticated/guest request can reach this handler and reset any known user's password, resulting in account takeover.
review.landing.exampleFindingRecommendation	Require a valid authenticated non-guest user for this route, verify `req.userId === req.body.username` for self-service changes (or require admin permission for resets), and verify the current password before writing the new password. Reject guest/unauthenticated requests and avoid disclosing whether arbitrary usernames exist if possible.
